# Task priority (ed.3 6.8.2: PRIORITY 0 is the highest; table 62,
# non-preemptive scheduling: among the tasks ready at the same time, the
# one with the highest priority is executed first). The writer (priority
# 0) runs before the reader (priority 1) in every step, so the reader sees
# the value written in the same step: seen = g. A runtime that runs tasks
# in declaration order would show seen one step behind (0, 10, 20, ...).
period_ms: 100
inputs:
outputs: g p_reader.seen
status: conformant
reference: IEC 61131-3 ed.3 6.8.2 (TASK PRIORITY, non-preemptive scheduling)
---
0 => g=10 p_reader.seen=10
1 => g=20 p_reader.seen=20
2 => g=30 p_reader.seen=30
3 => g=40 p_reader.seen=40
